    "text": "The Acquedotto Vergine, also known as the Aqua Virgo, is a historic Roman aqueduct that supplied water to ancient Rome and continues to provide water to many of the city's iconic fountains. Its engineering, longevity, and cultural significance make it a key monument of Roman hydraulic infrastructure.",
